<title>THAILAND: Mitsui Corp buys 540-mln baht of Thai commodities.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Corp buys 540-mln baht of Thai commodities.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Corp of Japan on Friday signed a counter trade agreement to buy 540 million baht ($20.8 million) worth of rice, rubber, tapioca, and other goods from Thailand, a senior commerce ministry official said.</p>
<p>Under the counter trade agreement, Mitsui will sell up to 18 billion baht worth of equipment to the state-run Electricity Generating Authority of Thailand, the official said.</p>
<p>Other products that Mitsui will buy from Thailand included frozen chicken, canned pineapple and furniture, he said.</p>
<p>The Thai government has encouraged state agencies to take counter trade deals in order to narrow the country's huge trade and current account deficit.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
